Retrieve specific user data content for a given pool.
Tip: add `?dl=1` at the end of the URL to directly retrieve the base64 decoded content of your user data.

USAGE:
  scw k8s pool get-userdata <pool-id ...> [arg=value ...]

EXAMPLES:
  Get a pool user data by name
    scw k8s pool get-userdata 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111 key=cloud-init

ARGS:
  pool-id           Pool the user data are associated to
  key               User data key to retrieved
  [region=fr-par]   Region to target. If none is passed will use default region from the config (fr-par | nl-ams | pl-waw | it-mil)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for get-userdata
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use
